# `SEQUENCE-GENRE-VOCABULARY`: `--` is a LINE ERROR on `message` and legal on every
# other connector spelling in the language. The operator set is per genre for
# the same reason the keywords are: a Message carries a sending AND a
# receiving event occurrence (UML 2.5.1 §17.4.3.1 defines the LOST case as the
# one where the receiving occurrence is absent), so a message with unstated
# direction is not a thing this domain has.
#
# The second section is the KEEP half, and it is what makes the claim a
# per-genre one rather than a language-wide retirement: the same operator on
# the same shared scanner still parses under `block`.
#
# The endpoint resolution error is here too, because it is the other thing a
# message line can get wrong: both endpoints must be declared `lifeline` ids.
figdown 0.4 sequence
lifeline c "C"
lifeline s "S"
message c -- s "no direction"
message c -[mid]- s
message c -> nobody "unknown endpoint"

figdown 0.1 block
node a "A"
node b "B"
edge a -- b
